\cf2 Psi (\uc0\u936 ) System Terms\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\uc0\u936  (Psi): A metric representing signal or transmission quality, used to quantify transmission efficacy.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Transmission Loss: The reduction in signal power during transmission, affecting data integrity.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Spectrum: The range of frequencies used for communication; monitoring spectrum ensures optimal data transmission.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Signal Strength: The power level of the received signal, indicating transmission quality.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Validation Metrics: Data points such as \uc0\u936 , transmission loss, spectrum, and signal strength, used to assess transmission reliability.\
